## Dev-database seeds

Development and worktree databases are provisioned **only from synthetic or irreversibly anonymized seed data — never raw production copies.** Anonymization must not be reversible from inside the dev environment (no re-identification key alongside the data). Each seed records its provenance (synthetic generator or anonymization run) so a reviewer can verify the source.

---

## Gate semantics and consumption contract

**General rule:** no feature that produces evidence artifacts may run against customer data until its build demonstrates conformance with this policy. "The rules exist" is necessary but not sufficient — the consuming build must show its capture/output/provisioning step implements them.

Build specs for artifact-producing features carry the matching gate language below, verbatim or strengthened:

- **Visual-evidence capture:** *"Capture applies the mask-at-capture region list (DATA-POLICY § Mask-at-capture) before any artifact is written. The reviewer checklist includes the no-unmasked-sensitive-region check. This build ships or schedules the 90-day purge for `results/visual-evidence/`. No runs against customer data until all three hold."*
- **Differential/oracle outputs:** *"Diff outputs reference entities by ID; any PII field is enumerated and justified in this spec; no raw sensitive personal data ever. This build ships or schedules the 90-day purge for `results/differential/`. No customer-data runs until these hold."*
- **Telemetry/logging:** *"Logs are PII-minimized and reference entities by ID. Per-feature attribution keys must not embed customer identifiers. 365-day retention with receipted purge. No customer-data runs until these hold."*
- **Dev-DB provisioning:** *"Worktree/dev databases are provisioned only per DATA-POLICY § Dev-database seeds — synthetic or irreversibly anonymized, provenance recorded, never raw production copies. No dev-database provisioning until these hold."*

The operator owns the gate: a build claiming conformance is verified against this document, not against its own report.
